WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.909
Scraps is a food-waste log for a household.

00:00:02.909 --> 00:00:08.335
You note what you throw away, and it shows the carbon and water it took to produce that food,

00:00:08.335 --> 00:00:10.960
so you can see which habit is worth changing.

00:00:11.963 --> 00:00:15.887
Logging takes a few taps: the food, how much, and why.

00:00:15.887 --> 00:00:19.883
Before you add it, Scraps shows what producing it took.

00:00:20.886 --> 00:00:25.611
Here is a made-up week for a household of two.

00:00:25.611 --> 00:00:33.930
2.03 kg of food thrown away took 14 kg CO2e and 1,259 litres of water to produce:

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:36.806
about 106 kg of food a year.

00:00:37.808 --> 00:00:43.530
The biggest lever is beef: only 90 g, but 63% of the week's footprint.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:48.598
Wasting half as much for a year would avoid about 233 kg CO2e.

00:00:48.598 --> 00:00:52.848
The tips match the food, and the most common reason.

00:00:53.849 --> 00:00:57.094
The chart ranks foods by footprint, where beef leads.

00:00:57.094 --> 00:01:00.889
Switch it to weight, and milk and potatoes come first instead.

00:01:01.892 --> 00:01:05.697
The figures are global averages from Poore and Nemecek,

00:01:05.697 --> 00:01:07.842
published by Our World in Data.

00:01:07.842 --> 00:01:12.132
Scraps runs in your browser, and the log stays on this device.
